SUMMARY:Alcohol Through the Lens of Motherhood
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Community Mom's Group\n**RSVPing on Meetup doesn’t
  reserve your spot for this session!**\n\nTo join\, please sign up through
  our site here:\nhttps://www.totem.org/spaces/session/sfi204exc/\n\nAll se
 ssions are free\, and signing up on the site helps us create a smoother ex
 perience for everyone.\nFeel free to message me with any questions or conc
 erns!\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\
 -\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\nFor many of us\, alcohol has played a role in
  some pretty meaningful memories. Holidays\, celebrations\, nights out wit
 h friends\, or even a drink at the end of a long day. For others\, it brin
 gs up memories we'd rather forget. And as we get older\, especially once w
 e become parents\, our relationships with alcohol can change in ways we di
 dn't expect.\n\nWith the holidays approaching\, we're exploring how alcoho
 l fits into our lives and families. From our own drinking habits to naviga
 ting how others drink around our children\, we'll talk about the tradition
 s\, boundaries\, and conversations that shape our experiences. Whether you
  drink\, don't drink\, or fall somewhere in between\, this session is an o
 pportunity to reflect on the relationship we have with alcohol and the one
  we hope our children will develop.\n\n**How It Works**\n\n* *Free and con
 fidential* – hosted on Totem’s secure platform\n* *Guided sharing* –
  everyone gets a turn\, no pressure to overshare\n* *Family-friendly* – 
 babies\, toddlers\, and background noise welcome\n\n**Meet Your Host**\nHi
 \, I’m Heather\, I am an Asheville-based mom of two\, full-time [Totem](
 https://www.totem.org) team member\, and passionate believer in Spaces whe
 re moms can be real\, seen\, and supported.
